From: shouchen <TheOneovb@petlover.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btqca: mark LE Read Transmit Power broken on WCN3990

The WCN3990 firmware on this board (soc 0x40010224, rom 0x1001, patched
with qca/crbtfw21.tlv) advertises LE Read Transmit Power (0x204b) in its
Read Local Supported Commands bitmap and then rejects the command with
"Unknown HCI Command" (0x01).

hci_le_read_tx_power_sync() guards that command on commands[38] bit 7
only, so it is sent, the status comes back as 0x01, and the whole LE
init stage aborts.  What that looks like from userspace, on raphael:

  hci0: BD Address: ...  ACL MTU: 0:0  SCO MTU: 0:0  DOWN
  hciconfig hci0 up -> Can't init device hci0: Function not
                       implemented (38)      (bt_to_errno() fallback
                                              for the unmapped status)
  bluetoothctl show -> No default controller available

btbcm and btusb already carry this quirk for controllers that lie about
that bit; do the same for wcn3990 here.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -995,7 +995,23 @@
 	err = qca_check_bdaddr(hdev, &config);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	/*
+	 * WCN3990 firmware on this board (rom 0x1001 + crbtfw21.tlv) lists
+	 * LE Read Transmit Power (0x204b) in its supported-commands bitmap
+	 * and then answers it with "Unknown HCI Command" (0x01).
+	 * hci_le_read_tx_power_sync() treats that as fatal, so the LE init
+	 * stage aborts and hci0 never comes up.  btbcm and btusb work
+	 * around the same lie with this quirk.
+	 */
+	switch (soc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3990:
+		hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_READ_TRANSMIT_POWER);
+		break;
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+
 	bt_dev_info(hdev, "QCA setup on UART is completed");
 
 	return 0;
